1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
SUSIE: Hello?

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,654
PAUL: Hi, Susie, it's Paul here.

3
00:00:05,654 --> 00:00:11,940
How are you? Enjoying your new job? You're working at the library, aren't you?

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:18,360
SUSIE: Yes. I started when the library re-opened a month ago. It's great.

5
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:22,760
PAUL: Actually Carol and I have been meaning to join for a while.

6
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:26,340
SUSIE: Oh, you should. It doesn't cost anything

7
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:29,841
and the new library has all sorts of facilities.

8
00:00:29,841 --> 00:00:33,590
It's not Just a place where you borrow books.

9
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:38,228
For instance, there's an area with comfortable seats where you can sit

10
00:00:38,228 --> 00:00:43,640
and read the magazines they have there. Some people spend the whole morning there.

11
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:48,050
PAUL: Mmm. Wish I had that amount of time to spend!

12
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:53,680
SUSIE: Yes, you must be pretty busy at present, with the children and everything?

13
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:58,000
PAUL: We are, yes. But we're hoping to get away this summer

14
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,810
We're thinking of going to Greece.

15
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:06,483
SUSIE: Well, we've got a much larger section of the library devoted to travel books now,

16
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:09,320
so you should come and have a look.

17
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:15,540
I can't remember if there's anything specifically on Greece, but I should think so.

18
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:21,481
PAUL: OK. Now Carol's organising a project for the history class she teaches at school -

19
00:01:21,481 --> 00:01:25,500
it's about life in the town a hundred years ago

20
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,610
Do you have anything that might be useful?

21
00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:32,822
SUSIE: Yes, actually we've now got a new section

22
00:01:32,822 --> 00:01:37,970
with materials on the history of the town and surrounding region.

23
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:44,107
PAUL: Right. I'll tell her. You can't always find that sort of thing on the internet.

24
00:01:44,107 --> 00:01:49,860
Now in the old library there used to be a separate room with reference books.

25
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:52,810
It was a really nice quiet room.

26
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:58,153
SUSIE: Yes, We've put those books in the main part of the library now,

27
00:01:58,153 --> 00:02:01,970
but we do have a room called the community room.

28
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:08,140
It can be hired out for meetings, but at other times people can use it to study.

29
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:13,500
PAUL: I might use that. It's hard to find anywhere quiet at home sometimes.

30
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:17,825
SUSIE: I can't remember how old your son and daughter are...

31
00:02:17,825 --> 00:02:22,151
we've introduced a special section of fiction written specially for teenagers,

32
00:02:22,151 --> 00:02:25,690
but they might be a bit young for that?

33
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:28,040
PAUL: Yes, they would be.

34
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:32,620
SUSIE: Well, we do have lots of activities for younger children.

35
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,250
PAUL: Yes?

36
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:37,340
SUSIE: For example we have a Science Club

37
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:41,411
At the next meeting, they're going to be doing experiments

38
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:46,980
with stuff that everyone has in the kitchen - sugar and flour and so on.

39
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:49,870
PAUL: They might be interested, yes.

40
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:54,362
SUSIE: And we have a competition for children called Reading Challenge.

41
00:02:54,362 --> 00:02:58,445
That doesn't begin until after the end of term.

42
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:04,570
They have to read six books, and they get a certificate if they manage it.

43
00:03:04,570 --> 00:03:07,060
PAUL: So that gives them something to do

44
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:10,320
while they're on holiday, instead of getting bored.

45
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:15,310
SUSIE: That's the idea. And there's special activities for adults too.

46
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:23,930
On Friday we have a local author called Tanya Streep who's going to be talking about her new novel.

47
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:26,280
It's called 'Catch the Mouse

48
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:32,300
and she based the story on a crime that actually took place here years ago.

49
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:37,520
PAUL: Right. We're not free on Friday, but I'll look out for the book.

50
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:40,260
SUSIE: Now this probably isn't for you

51
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:44,870
but we do have IT support available for members.

52
00:03:44,870 --> 00:03:48,284
PAUL: We get quite a few older people coming along

53
00:03:48,284 --> 00:03:52,380
who are wanting to get up to speed with computer technology.

54
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:58,880
It's on Tuesday mornings - they don't need to make an appointment or anything, they just turn up.

55
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:03,120
PAUL: Well, my mother might be interested, I'll let her know.

56
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:09,257
SUSIE: OK. And there's another service which you wouldn't expect from a library,

57
00:04:09,257 --> 00:04:12,090
which is a free medical check-up.

58
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:15,160
The hospital arranges for someone to come along

59
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:18,445
and measure the level of sugar in your blood,

60
00:04:18,445 --> 00:04:21,810
and they check cholesterol levels at the same time.

61
00:04:21,810 --> 00:04:23,340
PAUL: Really?

62
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:29,460
SUSIE: Yes, but that's only for the over-60s, so you wouldn't qualify.

63
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:34,340
PAUL: OK. Well, I'll tell my mother, she might be interested.

64
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:41,442
SUSIE: What other information... well, we do have a little shop with things like wallcharts

65
00:04:41,442 --> 00:04:45,120
and greetings cards, and also stamps

66
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:49,490
so you can post the cards straightaway, which is really useful.

67
00:04:49,490 --> 00:04:54,794
PAUL: Yeah. Well, I'll bring the children round at the weekend and we'll join.

68
00:04:54,794 --> 00:04:59,720
Oh, one more thing - I'll be bringing the car, is there parking available?

69
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:04,450
SUSIE: Yes. and it's free in the evening and at weekends.

70
00:05:04,450 --> 00:05:09,220
PAUL: Perfect. Well, thanks, Susie see you...
